Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:33:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] registry: architect_critic serving stays -t 96, canonical env
 (DAR-LAT-3h FALLBACK, outcome L only)

Merge ONLY if gate G1's verdict is L (neither recipe arm non-inferior to the
live configuration). recipe.threads 48 -> 96, recipe.cpu_shape -> NUMA_FULL,
and recipe.env renamed champion_measurement_env so nothing reads it as a
serving env. No launch change; no relaunch.

Unsigned. Part of the DAR-LAT-3h stack-change package
(epyc-root artifacts/operator/stack-change-dar-lat-3h-20260926/).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FKXdQsgLuwnFVWQ3npGfrJ
---
 orchestration/model_registry.yaml | 15 +++++++++------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/orchestration/model_registry.yaml b/orchestration/model_registry.yaml
index 5146e6b3..d419ddf5 100644
--- a/orchestration/model_registry.yaml
+++ b/orchestration/model_registry.yaml
@@ -1805,7 +1805,10 @@ server_mode:
       recipe_id: qwen38-flash-next-cpu-mtp
       module: epyc-inference-research/scripts/lib/qwen38_flash_next_recipe.py
       surface: cpu-decode
-      threads: 48        # on a 0-95 cpuset. = scripts/lib/qwen38_flash_next_recipe.py THREADS.
+      threads: 96        # on a 0-95 cpuset. 2026-09-26 DAR-LAT-3h gate G1 outcome L: the
+                         # SERVING -t is 96, re-derived from a served ABA on production v10 (the G1
+                         # receipt is the citation). The module's THREADS = 48 stays the champion
+                         # MEASUREMENT recipe's -t and is a different object.
                          # ⚠ CORRECTED 2026-09-26 (DAR-LAT-3h): this used to say "the SERVED decode
                          # optimum". No served 48-vs-96 comparison existed; the 48 rests on pre-BIOS
                          # bare llama-bench (D4/C5, tg128 t48 10.09 vs t96 9.67). The live :8074 ran
@@ -1814,7 +1817,7 @@ server_mode:
                          # (epyc-root, operator artifact dir stack-change-dar-lat-3h-20260926)
                          # decides; its receipt replaces this note. epyc-orchestrator tests/unit/
                          # test_critic_shape_recipe_parity.py now diffs this row against the topology.
-      cpu_shape: NUMA_FULL_T48
+      cpu_shape: NUMA_FULL      # was NUMA_FULL_T48 (lineup-change C3); superseded by the G1 receipt
       # ── C3 RESOLVED (operator ruling: "add the needed cpu shape") ─────────────────
       # An earlier draft recorded -t 48 on a 0-95 cpuset as an UNRESOLVED CONFLICT with
       # stack_numa._assert_instance_invariants, which raises at import when a non-GPU
@@ -1842,10 +1845,10 @@ server_mode:
       # shape changes the thread count and nothing else.
       no_mmap: true
       flash_attn: on
-      env:
-        # 2026-09-26 (DAR-LAT-3h): declared here since 2026-09-22 and NEVER READ by the launcher,
-        # so the live :8074 carried none of it. epyc-orchestrator stack_env._ROLE_ENV_BLOCKS
-        # ["architect_critic"] now emits it, and test_stack_env_recipe_parity.py diffs the two.
+      # 2026-09-26 DAR-LAT-3h gate G1 outcome L: the recipe env was NOT non-inferior when served,
+      # so it is not a serving env. Renamed from `env` so nothing reads it as one; the launcher
+      # keeps the canonical OMP stack + GGML_IQK=1 only.
+      champion_measurement_env:
         GGML_NOHUGEPAGE_PROCESS: "1"   # CHAMP-2, ADOPTED 2026-09-08 (operator-ruled).
                                        # UNIT = SESSION, set AT LAUNCH. cpu-decode ONLY —
                                        # R23-58 measured a bounded null on the GPU surface.
